## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-driven incentives in streaming, including how CKNE affects throughput, partitioning, and latency, plus a stable rebalancing loop and end-to-end validation.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-throughput/partition mapping
- Kafka partition rebalancing and windowing impact
- Baseline SLA guarantees with dynamic prioritization
- Telemetry, monitoring, and stability guarantees

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-mapping for CKNE-driven resource allocation
function mapCKNETokens(ckne, baseThroughput, basePartitions, kappa, lambda, minP, maxP){
  const T = baseThroughput * (1 + kappa * (ckne - 0.5));
  const P = Math.max(minP, Math.min(maxP, Math.round(basePartitions * (1 + lambda * (ckne - 0.5)))));
  return {throughput: T, partitions: P};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes CKNE-driven resource governance in a practical API gateway, testing token bucket logic, dynamic reallocation, fairness, SLA guarantees, telemetry, and testing.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE mapping to quotas
- Token bucket vs leaky bucket
- Minute granularity reallocation
- Fairness and baseline SLA
- Telemetry and test planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) { this.rate = rate; this.burst = burst; this.tokens = burst; this.last = Date.now(); }
  allow(n = 1) {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + this.rate * elapsed);
    this.last = now;
  }
}
```
